;; A deck that does not fit, and says what to do about it.
;;
;; Exists so the STATIC EXPORT path has coverage: `plato build` emits plain
;; Reveal HTML with no ClojureScript in it, so before the :fit bundle a slide
;; that declared {:overflow :shrink} had nothing to shrink it and nothing could
;; ask the page whether its slides fit. The e2e suite exports this deck and
;; drives the result.
;;
;; The slide has to genuinely overflow a 960x700 box for the check to mean
;; anything, and it has to overflow by little enough that fitting it stays above
;; plato.fit/min-scale — a slide needing less than 60% is a :too-small, which is
;; a different verdict and would not exercise the shrink.
{:title "Shrink"
 :slides
 [{:plato/type :slide
   :id :fits
   ;; A [:section ...] here would nest inside the slide's own <section>, which
   ;; is how a vertical stack is spelled — the id would land on the container
   ;; and the leaf plato.fit measures would have none.
   :content [:div [:h2 "This one fits"] [:p "So nothing is scaled."]]}

  {:plato/type :slide
   :id :too-tall
   :overflow :shrink
   :content
   [:div {:style {:height "800px"}} [:h2 "A deliberately overfull 800px fixture"] [:p "Its geometry, not font wrapping, makes it taller than the 700px slide box."]]}]}
